{{define "minimal"}}
## Minimal plan rule

The plan contains only the work needed for the agreed result while honouring the accepted constraints. Necessary preparation, verification and rollback are in scope. No side refactors, "while we are here" improvements, generalisation for the future, extra configurability or polish that the requirements do not ask for. Ideas beyond scope do not become steps or requirements; if something outside the task seems important, ask the user a question instead. An assumption you make to fill a gap stays the smallest reasonable choice and never adds a capability, a requirement or a step (for example, choosing where a value comes from must not add a way to override it). Minimal never means dropping an agreed requirement or constraint.
{{end}}

